WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.462
Sofia Lindqvist: Alright, it’s 10:01, let’s get started. Happy Friday, everyone!

2
00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:09.913
Kwame Asante: Morning! Hope everyone’s got coffee, I definitely needed mine today.

3
00:00:10.994 --> 00:00:14.840
Hannah Weiss: Hi all! I’m running on tea, but same energy, Kwame.

4
00:00:16.286 --> 00:00:20.516
Tomás Rivera: Good morning. I’m still catching up on emails, but I’m here.

5
00:00:21.232 --> 00:00:26.617
Grace Liu: Hey everyone! Sorry, I was just finishing up a call with the EMEA team.

6
00:00:27.746 --> 00:00:33.131
Sofia Lindqvist: No worries, Grace. Quick round of updates before we dive in—anything urgent from anyone?

7
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:38.430
Kwame Asante: Nothing urgent, just prepping for onboarding next week. We’ve got three new hires.

8
00:00:39.527 --> 00:00:44.143
Hannah Weiss: Absence requests are up a bit, probably summer holidays. Otherwise, all good.

9
00:00:45.158 --> 00:00:48.620
Tomás Rivera: Legal’s quiet, just reviewing some vendor contracts. Nothing major.

10
00:00:48.952 --> 00:00:53.183
Grace Liu: I’m working on the engagement survey follow-up, but that’s for later.

11
00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:59.003
Sofia Lindqvist: Great, thanks all. Let’s move to the main agenda: Confidentiality policy review.

12
00:01:00.308 --> 00:01:08.000
Kwame Asante: Yeah, so, we’ve had a couple questions from new hires about when exactly they need to sign the confidentiality agreement.

13
00:01:08.981 --> 00:01:14.750
Hannah Weiss: Right, and I noticed the policy just says 'upon commencement,' but doesn’t specify a deadline.

14
00:01:15.107 --> 00:01:23.953
Tomás Rivera: From a legal standpoint, it’s best if it’s signed before access to any sensitive info. But sometimes IT grants access on day one.

15
00:01:25.432 --> 00:01:31.586
Grace Liu: I’ve seen a few cases where folks started before their paperwork was fully processed, especially contractors.

16
00:01:32.804 --> 00:01:38.958
Sofia Lindqvist: So, should we clarify the timing? Like, require the agreement to be signed before system access?

17
00:01:39.609 --> 00:01:46.147
Kwame Asante: That makes sense. Maybe we say, 'must be signed prior to receiving any company credentials or access'?

18
00:01:46.904 --> 00:01:53.058
Hannah Weiss: Yeah, and maybe add a specific timeframe? Like, within 48 hours of receiving the offer letter?

19
00:01:53.740 --> 00:02:01.817
Tomás Rivera: I’d lean toward 'before access' as the hard requirement. The 48 hours is good, but access is the key legal point.

20
00:02:02.675 --> 00:02:09.598
Grace Liu: Agreed. We can work with IT to make sure access is only granted after the agreement is signed.

21
00:02:10.241 --> 00:02:20.241
Sofia Lindqvist: Okay, so update the policy to say: 'All team members must sign the Confidentiality Agreement before being granted access to any GitLab systems or confidential information.'

22
00:02:21.546 --> 00:02:26.930
Kwame Asante: Got it. I’ll update the handbook page and flag it for IT and onboarding.

23
00:02:28.199 --> 00:02:33.199
Hannah Weiss: Should we mention contractors specifically? Sometimes they’re a bit of a gray area.

24
00:02:33.537 --> 00:02:38.152
Tomás Rivera: Good point. Maybe just say 'team members and contractors' to be explicit.

25
00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:43.063
Grace Liu: Yeah, let’s add that. We’ve had confusion there before.

26
00:02:44.089 --> 00:02:54.858
Sofia Lindqvist: Alright, so the new text will read: 'All team members and contractors must sign the Confidentiality Agreement before being granted access to any GitLab systems or confidential information.'

27
00:02:56.135 --> 00:02:59.597
Kwame Asante: Perfect. I’ll make sure that’s clear in the update.

28
00:03:00.716 --> 00:03:04.563
Hannah Weiss: Thanks, Kwame. That should help clear up the onboarding questions.

29
00:03:05.329 --> 00:03:08.406
Tomás Rivera: And from legal, that covers us. Thanks, everyone.

30
00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:14.560
Grace Liu: Great, thanks all. Should we do a quick check-in on the unrelated item?

31
00:03:16.015 --> 00:03:17.553
Sofia Lindqvist: Yes, Grace, go ahead.

32
00:03:18.104 --> 00:03:24.258
Grace Liu: So, the engagement survey results are in. Participation was 87%, which is up from last quarter.

33
00:03:25.509 --> 00:03:27.432
Kwame Asante: Nice! That’s a big jump.

34
00:03:28.331 --> 00:03:31.793
Hannah Weiss: That’s awesome. Any big themes we should know about?

35
00:03:32.621 --> 00:03:39.545
Grace Liu: Mostly positive, but a few comments about communication during onboarding. I’ll pull together a summary for next week.

36
00:03:40.311 --> 00:03:44.157
Sofia Lindqvist: Thanks, Grace. Can you send us a one-pager by Wednesday?

37
00:03:45.307 --> 00:03:46.807
Grace Liu: Yep, will do.

38
00:03:47.356 --> 00:03:51.202
Tomás Rivera: Looking forward to seeing that. Always good to get feedback.

39
00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:56.356
Kwame Asante: Let me know if you need any onboarding data, Grace.

40
00:03:57.636 --> 00:04:00.713
Grace Liu: Thanks, Kwame, I might ping you for that.

41
00:04:01.025 --> 00:04:05.256
Sofia Lindqvist: Alright, I think that covers everything. Any last questions or comments?

42
00:04:06.602 --> 00:04:08.141
Hannah Weiss: Nope, all good here.

43
00:04:08.658 --> 00:04:10.158
Tomás Rivera: Nothing from me.

44
00:04:10.962 --> 00:04:15.193
Kwame Asante: I’m good. I’ll get started on the policy update after this.

45
00:04:16.186 --> 00:04:18.878
Grace Liu: All set. Have a great weekend, everyone!

46
00:04:19.571 --> 00:04:21.494
Sofia Lindqvist: Thanks, all. Enjoy your Friday!

47
00:04:21.731 --> 00:04:23.231
Kwame Asante: Bye!

48
00:04:24.538 --> 00:04:26.038
Hannah Weiss: Bye, everyone.

49
00:04:26.474 --> 00:04:27.974
Tomás Rivera: Take care.

50
00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:29.950
Grace Liu: Bye!

51
00:04:31.187 --> 00:04:33.495
Sofia Lindqvist: Meeting adjourned. See you next week.
